        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Fusion AT, Contemporary Empire Lever</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nFusion Hardware's Empire Door Lever is reminiscent of 1930's shapes like the Empire State building. Going with the saying: what is old is new again, the redolent shape of the door lever is a great way to add a little retro flair to your home but in a very contemporary way. It is available in brushed nickel, oil rubbed bronze, and polished chrome finishes. It will fit 1-1/4 inch to 2 inch thick doors and has an optional 2-3/8 inch or 2-3/4 inch backset.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Fusion AT Empire Lever:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solid Brass/Bronze Construction</li>\r\n<li>Cycle Tested to ANSI Standards</li>\r\n<li>\"Positive Stop\" lever spring mechanism</li>\r\n<li>Reversible Latchbolt in matching/coordinating finish</li>\r\n<li>Easy assembly with alignment block and rose posts</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for Empire Contemporary Door Lever Fusion AT:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 3-7/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Lever Projection: 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-1/4\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backsets: Either 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass or Bronze</li>\r\n<li>Standard Latch Rotation is 40 Degrees.</li>\r\n<li>Square corner latches and strike plates </li>\r\n<li>Lifetime Limited Warranty on workmanship, materials, and operation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on one side of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Dummy Set:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on both sides of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (Hall or Closet):</b> For doors that don't need locking.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (Bedroom or Bathroom):</b> For doors that could need locking.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>",
            "seo": {
                "title": "Empire Contemporary Lever, Fusion AT",
                "description": "Contemporary Empire Lever Fusion AT - Fusion Hardware's Empire Door Lever is reminiscent of 1930's shapes like the Empire State building. Going with the saying: what is old is new again, the redolent shape of the door lever is a great way to add a little retro flair to your home but in a very contemporary way. It is available in Brushed Nickel, Oil Rubbed Bronze, and Polished Chrome finishes. It will fit 1-1/4 inch to 2 inch thick doors and can be adjusted for either 2-3/8 inch or 2-3/4 inch backsets.",
